Mitcad's patch to OCCT 8.0.1, under OCCT's licence:
SPDX-License-Identifier: LGPL-2.1-only WITH OCCT-exception-1.0

Fillet: a tangent ride (1720) whose end vertex holds one more rounding,
the edge of a face the ride's stripe touches and the face at the end;
and a ride all along between two roundings whose contacts pass each other
on the face between without crossing (mitcad#1926, after 1720 and 1721).

A wall 2.5 wide whose top's edges are rounded with 2 and 1, an edge at an
end of the wall rounded too (with 0.5 or 1, at either side, at either
end): the vertex where the ride's stripe ends holds that rounding as
well. 1720 made no ride there (the ride's ends had to meet no other
stripe), and the pair was rolled on the larger one's contact line (0016):
another shape, valid, 4.5 mm3 more material. And the top of a horseshoe
tower 2.127 to 3 wide (2 + 1 at its apex) rounded along its inner edge
with 2 and its outer edge with 1: each rounding alone fits on the top, so
neither overflows it and no overlap was found; their contacts pass each
other on the top, touching at the apex, and the mitred ends at the legs'
fronts failed (the blends crossing each other).

- ChFi3d_Builder::rideEndCornerAllowed (RideOnBlend): an end of either
  stripe may hold one more stripe, a constant rounding of another radius
  whose edge there does not bound the face between, at a vertex of three
  sharp edges.
- ChFi3d_Builder::PerformTwoCornerAtRideEnd (from PerformTwoCorner, first):
  at a vertex of two stripes where one (the big) is a tangent ride's
  stripe whose side on the face between ends at a mere point on the face
  at the end, which is the other's (the small's) other face: as
  PerformTwoCornerbyInter's bevel of a big and a small blend whose pivot
  points differ, the small is cut by the big's blend from the crossing of
  their contacts on their common face to the point where the small's
  contact on the face at the end meets the big's blend; the big is cut by
  the small's blend up to there and by the face at the end from there to
  the ride's point, both curves put in the data structure on the big's
  surface and the second on the face at the end, its transition there
  FORWARD where the vertex's side, which goes, lies on its right about the
  surface's own normal. Two roundings of one radius are not made so (their
  blends' intersection at a square corner is singular).
- Compute, with 1721's part rides (once the stripes are computed, before
  the corners): a pair of constant roundings of one SurfData each, sharing
  a face, that 1721 does not ride and whose contacts on it pass each other
  all along without crossing (the rider's contact nowhere farther from the
  other edge than the other's contact, nearer somewhere, the two spanning
  the face alike: contactsPassAllAlong) is ridden all along (RideOnBlend);
  where that fails, both are computed on the faces of their edges again.
- RideOnBlend and RideOnBlendPart: the larger stripe's contact on its blend
  (the rider's contact) put in the period of the larger stripe's own
  p-curves (inPeriodOf): on a periodic blend surface (a torus round an
  arc) the walk on the support left it a period off and the face's wire
  was not closed.

A ride whose end corner the small rounding reaches past the ride's point
(the small's contact on the face at the end meeting the rider's blend, not
the larger one's: a corner of three blends) is not made so: the corner
fails as before.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_tangent_ride.cpp, test_wall_end_corners
(ctest geometry.fillet_tangent_ride): the wall 2.5 wide with an end's edge
rounded too (0.5 or 1, either side, one or both ends), a prism and a box,
both orders: valid, the volume within a millionth; and
geometry.fillet_top_chains, test_tower_top on the stored case
`fillet-wall-run-on`. It fails with this patch and 7 later patches that
change the same lines reverted together, so the test does not single this
patch out (shown 2026-11-20 by tools/occt-port-proof.py; the patches are
listed in third_party/vcpkg-ports/docs/opencascade-before-after.md).

Failures (mitcad#1986): the handler round the two stripes' computation
again fails the fillet (done false): a boundary that reports the failure.
